OpenPyCharm JavaScript and TypeScript

This independent native IntelliJ Platform LSP integration is OpenPyCharm code,
licensed under the repository LICENSE. It does not contain JetBrains proprietary
JavaScript/TypeScript implementation code or require a JetBrains IDE account.

The plugin uses the public LSP API of the pinned open-source IntelliJ Platform.
Node.js 24.22.3, typescript-language-server 6.1.0 and TypeScript 6.0.3 are supplied
as an external pinned runtime under runtime/{target}, authenticated before use.
No dependency installation or automatic runtime download is performed.

Original tools.lock.json is retained as META-INF/frontend-tools.lock.json. Its
historical M0 product/packaging fields describe the original research lock, not
this product's default enablement or package layout. The pinned payloads and
licenses remain unchanged. Node.js's LICENSE contains its third-party notices;
TypeScript and typescript-language-server retain their Apache-2.0 licenses.
The runtime notices/ directory retains the original legal texts and package
metadata for all 21 packages embedded in the language-server CLI. The CLI source
map, package manifests, source URLs, versions and hashes are retained as pinned.

Normal project trust controls process startup. Analysis uses an isolated child
environment and project-scoped IDE system state; external Git/npm/service
authentication and the user's global Node configuration are not modified.
